            "topic": "Engineering Economics",
            "title": "Modified Internal Rate of Return (MIRR)",
            "question": "An investment of $10,000 yields $4,000 at the end of Year 1 and $8,000 at the end of Year 2. If the reinvestment rate is 10% and the finance rate is 8%, what is the Modified Internal Rate of Return (MIRR) over the 2-year period?",
            "options": [
                {
                    "label": "A",
                    "text": "$12.50\\%$",
                    "is_correct": false
                },
                {
                    "label": "B",
                    "text": "$11.35\\%$",
                    "is_correct": true
                },
                {
                    "label": "C",
                    "text": "$10.00\\%$",
                    "is_correct": false
                },
                {
                    "label": "D",
                    "text": "$8.45\\%$",
                    "is_correct": false
                }
            ],
            "solution": {
                "steps": [
                    {
                        "title": "Calculate Terminal Value of Cash Inflows",
                        "content": "The Year 1 inflow ($4000) is reinvested for 1 year at 10%: $4000 \\times 1.10 = 4400$. The Year 2 inflow is $8000$. Total Terminal Value (TV) = $4400 + 8000 = 12400$."
                    },
                    {
                        "title": "Calculate Present Value of Cash Outflows",
                        "content": "The only outflow is at Year 0, so Present Value (PV) = $10,000."
                    },
                    {
                        "title": "Calculate MIRR",
                        "content": "Use the formula: $PV \\times (1 + MIRR)^n = TV \\implies 10000(1 + MIRR)^2 = 12400$. $(1 + MIRR)^2 = 1.24 \\implies 1 + MIRR = \\sqrt{1.24} = 1.11355$. MIRR = $11.35\\%$."
                    }
                ],
                "solution_image": "",
                "video_explanation": "",
                "final_answer": "B"
            },
