            "topic": "Groundwater Flow",
            "title": "Darcy's Law in 3D",
            "question": "In a homogeneous, isotropic unconfined aquifer, the steady-state groundwater flow equation (Boussinesq equation) neglecting recharge is best approximated by which of the following expressions for the hydraulic head $h$?",
            "options": [
                {
                    "label": "A",
                    "text": "$\\nabla^2 (h^2) = 0$",
                    "is_correct": true
                },
                {
                    "label": "B",
                    "text": "$\\nabla^2 h = 0$",
                    "is_correct": false
                },
                {
                    "label": "C",
                    "text": "$\\nabla h = 0$",
                    "is_correct": false
                },
                {
                    "label": "D",
                    "text": "$\\frac{\\partial h}{\\partial t} = \\nabla^2 h$",
                    "is_correct": false
                }
            ],
            "solution": {
                "steps": [
                    {
                        "title": "Recall Darcy's Law",
                        "content": "Flux $q = -K \\nabla h$. For an unconfined aquifer, the transmissivity $T = K h$, meaning it varies with head."
                    },
                    {
                        "title": "Apply Continuity Equation",
                        "content": "For steady-state flow without recharge, $\\nabla \\cdot (T \\nabla h) = 0 \\implies \\nabla \\cdot (Kh \\nabla h) = 0$."
                    },
                    {
                        "title": "Simplify using Isotropic Assumption",
                        "content": "Since $K$ is constant, it cancels out. $h \\nabla h = \\frac{1}{2} \\nabla (h^2)$. Therefore, $\\nabla \\cdot \\nabla (h^2) = 0$, which simplifies to Laplace's equation for $h^2$: $\\nabla^2 (h^2) = 0$."
                    }
                ],
                "solution_image": "",
                "video_explanation": "",
                "final_answer": "A"
            },
